        <mxCell id="9FxaDju-jmE1-ypzIo4e-3" value="After the Infrastructure set up phase:&lt;br&gt;1. Serilog is split by different type (Audit, module, system, operation) and Enrich with traceID&lt;br&gt;trade id include Guid assign to the active user (issue during the first time they log in) and the source (External for client, internal for module)&lt;br&gt;2.Single nodeRedis have outbox (for handle failure) - so it have ability to heal connection drop, redis restart and allow for intervention&lt;br&gt;during outage (by recover module)&lt;br&gt;3. Rabit&amp;nbsp; Mq is splitting to different exchange base off of domain. they will have DLQ on demand (requrie by business requirement)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;---&lt;br&gt;For current loging: each new login will cache the user as active (with ttl until flag as log out) - no Access / refresh machanism yet.&lt;br&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
